 "_doc": "The landscape (sim/nature, api/nature_loader.cpp). weather: limits and defaults. wind 0-30 m/s reaches Beaufort 11 (28.5-32.6 m/s, WMO No. 8 annex). rain and thunder are shares; lightning, strikes a minute. current 0-4 m/s: lowland rivers run under 3 m/s (USGS, stream gauging). mist_height_m and gully_auto are modelling choices. clouds: span_m the sky's period (10 240 m, the largest map the medium town fills), height_m the cumulus base (the lifting condensation level seen over a city, 32-960 m as the tool allows), size_m and density modelling choices compared with reference-minha photos. fog: height_m a radiation fog 2-160 m deep (WMO Aerodrome Reports and Forecasts, shallow fog under 2 m, deep over 100 m), fog_texel_m the window's texel. paint: kinds in the card order of the Ground tab; strength_scale turns the brush's percent into a dab; rock_reach the rock laid past a landform's dab so it reaches the foot of its cliff (modelling). trees: density per hectare comes from the brush; models are two oaks, two cypresses, two palms. ecology: formations are densities 0..1 of each stratum, written from the field descriptions of the fitofisionomias (IBGE, Manual Tecnico da Vegetacao Brasileira, 2012; Ribeiro & Walter 1998 for the cerrado) as modelling choices; riparian_near and far the strip of forest along water (Lei 12.651/2012 art. 4 I a: 30 m at least); flat and steep degrees: relief classes of Embrapa (suave ondulado under 8 %, forte ondulado 20 %, escarpado over 75 % = 37 degrees); forest_line the altitude the high grasslands start at, scaled to this map's relief.",
